00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:40.060
So, to understand what will happen next season,
we need to remember that by the very end Joe

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:42.040
isn't in love with Love anymore.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:47.140
After she revealed her true nature to Joe,
his romantic illusion was shattered, and when

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:51.730
Love refused to let Joe out of the cage, he
said to himself that he would do what Beck

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:54.440
did to him and "pretend" to love her.

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:56.090
"What did Beck do in this situation?

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.620
[Beck] I love you.

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:58.620
[Joe] Right.

00:10:58.620 --> 00:10:59.620
She pretended to love me.

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:02.420
You're asking me to see you, to love you.

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:03.740
I don't know what to feel, Love.

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:05.480
But I know what to do."

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:10.010
In fact, Joe almost kills Love, until she
reveals that she's pregnant and carrying his

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:11.010
baby.

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:14.890
This is the only thing that stopped him from
murdering her, as protecting children is something

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:17.120
that Joe responds to in particular.

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:21.100
He went out of his way in both seasons, even
putting himself in danger, to protect both

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:22.700
Paco and Ellie.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:26.260
And he even tried to help Delilah perhaps
because of what Henderson did to her as a

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:27.260
child.

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:31.380
This all probably relates back to how Joe
feels about his own troubled childhood and

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:34.210
so he sympathises with children and wants
to help them.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:38.070
At the end of the season, this is how Joe
sees himself:

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:41.400
"I'm ready to be the good father I never had.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.420
To make the family I always dreamed of.

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:44.960
The one she deserves."

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:49.180
However, whether Joe really sticks around
is immediately undermined at the very end

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:52.300
as we see him beginning to stalk the woman
next door.

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:56.860
We know he believes he's trapped himself in
a cage with Love, so it's quite likely he

00:11:56.860 --> 00:12:01.550
will try and escape, perhaps with his daughter
even, and run to somewhere far from LA.

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:06.150
For anyone who isn't already aware, this TV
show is based on the books "You" and "Hidden

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:11.440
Bodies" by author Caroline Kepnes and she
already has two new books planned in the series.

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:15.950
According to EW, "the third book will see
Joe move to the Pacific Northwest with a plan

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:18.810
to become a family man in his own unique way."

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:23.800
Now, the TV show has deviated from the books
in various significant ways, but if Joe needs

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:28.630
to leave LA in a hurry, say because Love catches
him creeping on their neighbour, and tries

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:33.510
to kill him, then fleeing to another state
feels like something he would do, given that's

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:36.580
what he did when Candace returned to confront
him in New York.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:40.890
He might also run off with his daughter to
get her away from the clutches of the powerful

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:42.670
and corrupt Quinn family.

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:46.740
And remember that he's still in contact with
Will in Manila who could help him get set

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:49.800
up with new identities in a new location.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:54.180
And given the popularity of the show, I can't
see the showrunners wanting to end Joe's story

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:58.350
in the third season either, especially as
there is at least a fourth book planned in

00:12:58.350 --> 00:12:59.350
the series.

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:03.740
Which means, that I expect it's unlikely Joe
will see justice for any of his crimes until

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:08.960
season 4, at which point perhaps Candace's
prediction will eventually come true.

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:13.740
"Murder has a way of following you,
and you're not getting away with it."

